.TH AUDIO_STREAMER 1 "2026-11-02" "nanokvm-audio-streamer 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
audio_streamer \- stream a NanoKVM / LicheeRV Nano MEMS microphone over HTTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B audio_streamer
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B audio_streamer
captures mono 16-bit PCM from an ALSA capture device and serves it to any
number of HTTP clients as a lossless WAV (LPCM) stream.
.PP
On the Sipeed NanoKVM (LicheeRV Nano) the onboard MEMS microphone is card 0,
device 0 (\fIhw:0,0\fR), at 48 kHz mono. The microphone hears the room around
the KVM, not the HDMI audio of the controlled host.
.PP
The stream is unauthenticated. Run it on a trusted network only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIN\fR
TCP port to listen on (default 8080).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-address " " \fIA\fR
IPv4 address to bind (default 0.0.0.0).
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-device " " \fID\fR
ALSA capture device (default hw:0,0). See \fBarecord \-l\fR.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rate " " \fIN\fR
Requested sample rate in Hz (default 48000). The nearest rate supported by
the hardware is used and reported in the stream.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-channels " " \fIN\fR
Channel count (default 1).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-period " " \fIN\fR
ALSA period in milliseconds (default 20).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Detach and run in the background. Not needed under systemd.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log connections, overruns and errors to standard error.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B /
Returns an \fIaudio/wav\fR stream: an HTTP 200, a 44-byte WAV header with
unknown length (0xFFFFFFFF), then continuous PCM.
.TP
.B /healthz
Returns a JSON status document, for example:
.RS
.PP
.nf
{"status":"ok","device":"hw:0,0","rate":48000,"channels":1,
 "clients":1,"served":3,"uptime_s":412}
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Listen in a browser:
.PP
.nf
    http://192.168.1.27:8080/
.fi
.PP
Capture ten seconds to a file:
.PP
.nf
    ffmpeg \-i http://192.168.1.27:8080/ \-t 10 capture.wav
.fi
.PP
Run on a different port with logging:
.PP
.nf
    audio_streamer \-p 9090 \-v
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/nanokvm-audio-streamer
Options passed to the service through the \fBOPTIONS\fR variable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR arecord (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
